wed as a direction from the camera. Taking the dot product between the light direction and the vertex gives you a distance along the light direction. \n\nThis new code doesn't really have the same geometric interpretation. The dot product between the camera direction in world space, and the vertex position in world space offset by the camera position isn't really a meaningful value","created_at":"2026-01-15T20:04:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T20:04:25Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114961#discussion_r2695781641","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114961","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2695781641"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114961#discussion_r2695781641"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114961"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2695781641/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":2358,"original_line":2358,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":69,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2698960994","pull_request_review_id":3671444864,"id":2698960994,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6g3uBi","diff_hunk":"@@ -2342,8 +2354,9 @@ void fragment_shader(in SceneData scene_data) {\n \t\t\t\t\t\t\tvec4 pssm_coord = (directional_lights.data[i].shadow_matrix3 * v);\n \t\t\t\t\t\t\tpssm_coord /= pssm_coord.w;\n \n-\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfloat range_pos = dot(directional_lights.data[i].direction, v.xyz);\n-\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfloat range_begin = directional_lights.data[i].shadow_range_begin.z;\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\tvec3 v_world_camera_rel = vertex_interp_cam_relative + (v.xyz - vertex);\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfloat range_pos = dot(light_dir_world, v_wor